            <ArticleTitle>[ECG changes and angina pectoris due to direct current from a defective cardiac pacemaker].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>556-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case of a 73-year-old patient whose external cardiac pacemaker produced a constant direct current is reported. The patient had severe angina pectoris, and the ECG showed marked QT prolongation and deformation both of the QRS complex and of the ST-T segments. Both angina and ECG changes disappeared when the defective pacemaker was replaced.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
